# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Vite

> Generated: {{GENERATION_DATE}} | Claude Craft v{{VERSION}}

## What (Stack & Structure)

**Stack**: Vite {{VITE_VERSION}}, TypeScript {{TS_VERSION}}

**Scope**: framework-agnostic Vite usage only — vanilla JS/TS apps, library authoring (build.lib), multi-page apps (rollupOptions.input), Workers/WASM entries. Not for React/Vue/Angular/Svelte dev-server config — see that stack's own tooling.md.

### Project Structure
```
project-root/
├── index.html            # Entry point (SPA) — never move to public/
├── pages/                 # Additional HTML entries (multi-page apps)
│   ├── about.html
│   └── admin/
│       └── index.html
├── public/                # Static assets copied as-is (favicon, robots.txt) — NOT index.html
├── src/
│   ├── main.ts             # Vanilla app entry (SPA/MPA)
│   ├── index.ts             # Library entry (build.lib mode)
│   ├── workers/             # Worker entry points (new URL(...import.meta.url))
│   └── wasm/                 # WASM modules (?init / ?url imports)
├── vite.config.ts
├── vitest.config.ts        # Or a `test` field merged into vite.config.ts
└── tsconfig.json
```

## Why (Purpose & Organization)

### Architecture: {{ARCHITECTURE_PATTERN}}
- **Entry point**: `index.html` at the project root (or `root`), never inside `public/`
- **Library mode**: `build.lib` + `vite-plugin-dts` for packages published to npm
- **Multi-page**: `build.rollupOptions.input` naming each HTML entry explicitly
- **Workers/WASM**: `new Worker(new URL(...), { type: 'module' })`, `?init`/`?url` suffixes

See `rules/02-architecture.md` for complete patterns.

### Critical Rules
| Rule | Reason |
|------|--------|
| index.html never in public/ | Ensures module graph, HMR, and asset hashing |
| TypeScript strict + moduleResolution: "bundler" | Type safety aligned with Vite/esbuild resolution |
| Externalize peer deps in library mode | Avoids duplicated runtime for consumers |
| 80%+ coverage | Quality assurance |

